ly resolved\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0012\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0012\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"cross-check all foundation ownership, dependencies, and gates before accepting the wave\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0012 and correct only its documentation contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documentation concludes the foundation slice without claiming implementation or approval\",\"gated save work remains visible\"]}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..543c7f88926cb5e60da0ecd6c16f2cf49c3dec70\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0004\n+sequence: 4\n+title: Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\n+dependencies:\n+  - R0002\n+  - R0003\n+requirement_ids:\n+  - REQ-0001\n+  - REQ-0003\n+  - REQ-0004\n+  - REQ-0006\n+  - NFR-0002\n+  - NFR-0010\n+source_specifications:\n+  - specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\n+  - specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\n+source_catalogue_ids:\n+  - IMP-0004\n+authoring_batch: B0003\n+factory_stages:\n+  - F011\n+  - F012\n+  - F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; state envelopes deliberately exclude authored content.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the immutable, versioned shared campaign-state, command, result, event,\n+revision, interaction-ID, and deterministic-RNG contracts needed to validate\n+legal transitions. This foundation defines envelopes and invariants only; it\n+does not introduce a feature state machine or authored campaign values.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 provides the shared-core/adapter seam and R0003 provides deterministic\n+fixtures. They are implementation dependencies, not authoring blockers.\n+Retain GATE-0004: concrete party and content shapes remain unapproved.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/`.\n+- The versioned campaign-snapshot envelope and deterministic RNG state.\n+- The public core command, state, event, result, revision, and interaction-ID\n+  interfaces, plus `tests/core/contract.*`.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Make state transitions pure and explicit: a command carries an expected\n+campaign revision and stable interaction/action ID; processing returns either\n+a typed rejection with no mutation or ordered state/events with a new revision.\n+Validate command shape, session state, identifiers, availability, eligibility,\n+predicates, and expected revision before any transition. Invariant helpers\n+must reject invalid state and preserve the prior immutable state.\n+\n+Record deterministic RNG seed/state at safe boundaries. Require idempotency for\n+retries: a duplicate interaction ID or acknowledged durable transition returns\n+its prior result without a second reward, checkpoint, or revision-changing\n+transition. Process one command at a time per active campaign and reject stale\n+writers so visibility changes, repeated input, and concurrent tabs cannot\n+interleave a transition.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and PWA adapters submit the same shared command envelopes and consume the\n+same state/event results. Platform adapters may debounce controls and manage a\n+local slot lease/read-only warning, but neither gains authority to mutate state\n+directly. Installation, cache lifecycle, and storage-driver work are outside\n+this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not author content values; implement combat, inventory, quest, exploration,\n+or UI state machines; select party shapes; implement a save driver or cache;\n+add account, identity, token, role, network, or remote state; or create assets,\n+audio, maps, dialogue, or reference-derived content.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: these serializable state and interface\n+contracts deliberately exclude authored content. Do not create or reserve\n+incidental visual, source, audio, font, icon, illustration, texture, sprite,\n+map, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use R0003 deterministic fixtures to prove invalid commands leave the exact\n+  prior state unchanged and stale revisions reject without mutation.\n+- Prove a duplicate interaction ID returns the recorded prior outcome and\n+  produces no additional durable transition.\n+- Exercise controlled RNG state twice and compare state/event results.\n+- Exercise sequential command handling and a stale-writer fixture without\n+  selecting a browser-storage implementation.\n+- Record GATE-0004 as retained before adding concrete party/content shapes.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain contract-test output for invalid, stale, duplicate, deterministic-RNG,\n+and serialized transition cases, plus the public envelope/invariant inventory\n+and the retained GATE-0004 record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Invalid or stale commands cannot mutate campaign state.\n+- Duplicate interaction IDs are idempotent and cause no extra durable\n+  transition.\n+- State, command, result, event, revision, and RNG contracts are shared-core\n+  only, versioned where serialized, and independent of concrete content,\n+  persistence drivers, or connected scope.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a23dc319d401b46d4b0d77b57c5fedac12f65f2e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,116 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0008\n+sequence: 8\n+title: Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\n+dependencies:\n+  - R0002\n+  - R0004\n+requirement_ids:\n+  - REQ-0013\n+  - REQ-0014\n+  - REQ-0015\n+  - NFR-0012\n+source_specifications:\n+  - specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\n+source_catalogue_ids:\n+  - IMP-0008\n+authoring_batch: B0003\n+factory_stages:\n+  - F011\n+  - F012\n+  - F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; a negative scope boundary.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Document and test the P0 negative boundary: local campaign start, save, and\n+resume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, authorization\n+role, entitlement, multiplayer, moderation, safety, or connected service.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 supplies the core/adapter dependency seam and R0004 supplies the local\n+campaign state envelope. They are implementation dependencies. Retain\n+GATE-0006 / DEC-0006: no connected feature may be implemented until its scope,\n+privacy, security, operational, cost, and failure-mode decisions are approved.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `docs/security-boundary.md`.\n+- `tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*`.\n+- The future connected-service approval checklist and local-slot identity\n+  contract.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+State that the local browser profile is the P0 player boundary, not an account\n+or authorization guarantee. The local campaign is the source of truth and has\n+no remote profile, analytics stream, purchase ledger, match state, cloud\n+backup, role, privilege, or entitlement. Local slot selection is an opaque\n+local reference only and must not contain identity, token, privilege, or remote\n+profile fields.\n+\n+Add negative contract tests and a static boundary scan for P0 foundation\n+modules. They must fail on identity/token/role/entitlement fields, network or\n+server clients, sign-in/OAuth/sync paths, multiplayer/safety/moderation APIs,\n+purchase flows, or remote campaign authority. Treat future replication, if\n+ever approved, as a separate optional mirror rather than campaign truth.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA use the same local-slot contract and same\n+connected-scope exclusion. PWA installation, cache, and browser-origin storage\n+do not imply identity, authorization, sync, or a remote service. No target\n+obtains a distinct connected implementation path.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not implement sign-in, OAuth, accounts, profiles, tokens, roles,\n+authorization, synchronization, server APIs, analytics transport, multiplayer,\n+moderation, reporting, purchases, entitlements, cloud saves, remote\n+diagnostics, or security claims about a device owner. Do not create product\n+assets, audio, or connected-service configuration.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is documentation and negative test\n+coverage for an architectural exclusion. Do not create or reserve incidental\n+visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or\n+other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run a static scan across P0 foundation modules for prohibited identity,\n+  token, privilege, entitlement, and network/server-client fields or imports.\n+- Run negative fixtures that attempt prohibited connected-scope configuration\n+  and prove the contract rejects or does not expose it.\n+- Verify start, local save, and local resume fixtures require only a local slot\n+  reference and no remote request or account data.\n+- Review `docs/security-boundary.md` against the exclusion list and record\n+  GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 as retained for any future connected proposal.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain static-scan and negative-fixture results, local start/save/resume test\n+output showing no remote request, the security-boundary review, and the future\n+connected-service approval checklist with its retained gate.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- P0 start, save, and resume expose no identity, token, role, entitlement,\n+  remote-profile, or network-client field or dependency.\n+- Negative tests prevent connected-service scope from entering P0 foundation\n+  modules for both web and PWA delivery paths.\n+- Any future connected work remains outside campaign truth and blocked by\n+  GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 rather than implicitly approved.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"repairable_failure\",\"summary\":\"Authored R0004 and R0008 and checkpointed B0003 after targeted contract validation. The supplied structural validator cannot run because its front-matter parser crashes on list metadata.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"],\"test_result\":\"PASS: targeted Python validation confirmed both runbooks load and match manifest metadata, dependencies, requirement IDs, provenance, asset/audio assessments, required sections, and B0003 accepted checkpoint. PASS: git diff --check for the modified tracked manifest. BLOCKED: `python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0003` crashes in its existing front-matter parser with `AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'append'`.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Both assigned paths were absent before authoring; no conflicting R ID/path was overwritten or reused.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"Targeted validation printed: PASS: B0003 R0004/R0008 metadata, sections, provenance, dependencies, asset/audio assessments, and checkpoint match.\",\"browser_log\":\"Not applicable: both runbooks declare browser_impact: not_applicable.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Exactly R0004 and R0008 are authored for their allocated IMP records.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Created only `projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md` for IMP-0004 and `R0008.md` for IMP-0008.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Both outputs are small, dependency-correct, fully traceable contracts with explicit no-asset assessments.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Targeted validation matched dependencies, requirement IDs, manifest provenance, no-asset/no-audio metadata, and all required contract sections.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Conflicting existing work stops authoring without overwrite or ID reuse.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Pre-write discovery found neither assigned R path existed; only their allocated IDs were authored.\"},{\"criterion\":\"The manifest is checkpointed only after both outputs load and match it.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Both outputs loaded and matched the manifest in targeted validation; B0003 is now `accepted` with a validation checkpoint.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0003.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0002.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"],\"summary\":\"The requested R-series implementation-contract documentati